# Wave W17-R (Route 126): crater sand — crater-bay sand: a grey-warm bay sand under the crater wall, stone-grey flecks ground into it from the wall’s own falls (design: the Craterlake water — the crater wall rising huge south, its falls dropping into the sink). Route 126’s own sand — greyer and warmer at once than Route 125’s bright tide-banded sand: the bay in the crater’s shadow keeps the wall’s colour in its shore.
